{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Playwright-style auto-waiting interaction: waits for the target to be attached, visible, enabled (and bounding-box stable for click/check/uncheck), then dispatches. The wait loop is RUST-side (one eval cannot wait — the mechanism is a synchronous JS::Evaluate -> JSON.stringify, so a promise rval stringifies to {}); each poll tick is a self-contained eval that resolves/checks/dispatches in one synchronous task. Actions: click, fill (native setter, React-safe), type (per-char keydown/input/keyup), press (Enter/Tab/Escape/arrows/+chords; Enter requestSubmits), select (by value/label/text), check, uncheck. Selector engine beyond CSS: text=, role=, xpath=, css=, :has-text(), :visible, :nth-match(n), and >> chaining (e.g. \"form >> text=Save\"); same-origin iframes are walked. arg carries the value for fill/type, the key for press, the option for select; pass \"\" when unused. timeout_ms<=0 defaults to 10000. Returns {status, action, selector, desc, bbox, attempts, elapsed_ms, typed?/selected?/already?} or {status:err, msg, state(absent|hidden|disabled|stabilizing|no-option|error|channel), attempts, elapsed_ms}.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse flowlang::rand::rand_range;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;","params":[{"name":"action","type":"String"},{"name":"selector","type":"String"},{"name":"arg","type":"String"},{"name":"timeout_ms","type":"Integer"}],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"mqgnnp1a10bcf38a1j18d","readers":[],"time":1791203618100,"username":"system","writers":[]}